+# CP-6 handoff
+
+## Request
+Committee challenge and portfolio debate for Northbridge Synthetic Group (nbg), as of 2025-03-31. SYNTHETIC FIXTURE.
+
+## Sources
+
+| Source | Use |
+| --- | --- |
+| NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf | Maturity profile. |
+
+## Findings
+
+### Bottom line
+
+The committee should hold a neutral bias: refinancing risk outweighs the earnings record until the nearest maturity is funded.
+Basis: Fundamental credit (CP-2); Refinancing & LME (CP-3C)
+
+### Key findings
+
+- The bear case wins on refinancing: USD 336 million must be raised inside two years with no committed source.
+Basis: Refinancing & LME (CP-3C)
+- The portfolio posture is Requires More Work, because no mandate or exposure data were supplied, so the binding portfolio constraint is not established.
+
+### Contrary evidence and what would change the view
+
+A signed revolver extension would move the bias to positive.
+Basis: Refinancing & LME (CP-3C)
+
+### Limitations
+
+- No mandate or exposure data were supplied, so the portfolio posture cannot reach a size.
+
+### Committee challenge
+
+The bull case rests on earnings consistency; the bear case on the funding need, and the bear case is better evidenced.
+Basis: Fundamental credit (CP-2)
+
+### Portfolio posture
+
+Final Sizing Posture: Requires More Work. The decision is driven by the absence of mandate and exposure data, because no portfolio limit is supplied, which implies the size cannot be set.
+Basis: NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 43
+
+The binding portfolio constraint is data quality: the mandate and exposure report that would set a limit were not supplied.
+
+### T6A.4 — Bear cross-examination
+
+| Bull claim attacked | Bear counter-evidence | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Earnings are stable | USD 646 million matures inside two years | NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 43 |
+
+### T6A.7 — Debate resolution
+
+| Disputed risk | Resolution |
+| --- | --- |
+| Refinancing | Bear sustained |
+
+### T6E.4 — Compliance cross-examination
+
+| RV bullet attacked | Compliance counter-evidence | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Spread pickup | Not supplied: no mandate or exposure data | NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf |
+
+### T6E.6 — CIO evidence weighting
+
+| Dimension | Score | CIO assessment |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Mandate compliance | Not supplied: no mandate data | Not scored. |
+
+### T6E.7 — Allocation decision matrix
+
+| Disputed risk | Resolution |
+| --- | --- |
+| Mandate fit | Insufficient Information |
+
+### T6E.11 — Gaps ledger (portfolio debate)
+
+| Gap ID | Gap | Required follow-up |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| CP-6A-GAP-001 | No mandate or exposure report | Supply the fund's mandate and exposure report. |
+
+## Calculations
+None.
+
+## Gaps
+
+| Gap | Effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| No mandate or exposure report | The portfolio posture cannot reach a size. |
